<title>UK: Credit Lyonnais Rouse opens Tokyo office.</title>
<headline>Credit Lyonnais Rouse opens Tokyo office.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>London Metal Exchange (LME) ring dealers Credit Lyonnais Rouse (CLR) said on Friday that it had opened an office in Tokyo, appointing Takashi Saka as its head representative.</p>
<p>In a release CLR, a subsidiary of French bank Credit Lyonnais, said that Saka had managed Metallgesellschaft's Tokyo operations since 1991.</p>
<p>&quot;Initially I expect to be focusing on LME business, but the attraction of a firm such as CLR is the ability to develop related business,&quot; Saka said.</p>
<p>CLR Chairman Roy Leighton said, &quot;Japan is an important metals market and his (Saka's) appointment as the head of our new representative office further strengthens our presence there.&quot;</p>
<p>--London Newsroom 44 171 542 8080</p>
</text>
